# Security rules (mandatory)

## Secrets

| Variable | Where | Never |
|----------|-------|-------|
| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | `.env` server | `VITE_*`, client imports |
| `DATABASE_URL` | `.env` server | Client bundle |
| `SCANLOGIC_API_SECRET` | `.env` + Settings session | `VITE_*`, localStorage |

## HTTP

- All `/api/*` from browser: `apiFetch()` in `src/lib/apiFetch.js`.
- Remote/LAN: Bearer token must match server `SCANLOGIC_API_SECRET`.

## XSS

```jsx
// ✅
import SafeMarkdown from '@/components/SafeMarkdown'
<SafeMarkdown>{llmContent}</SafeMarkdown>

// ❌
<div dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: llmContent }} />
```

## SSRF (LLM images)

- `lib/security/safeUrl.js` — `isSafeFetchUrl()` before fetching user URLs in `anthropic.js`.
- Allow `https:` (public) and `data:image/*;base64,` only.

## Passwords (ScanVault)

- Hash with `hashPassword` / verify with `verifyPassword` in `lib/security/password.js`.
- Legacy plaintext: constant-time compare + migrate to hash on successful login.

## Share tokens

- `secureToken()` / UUID v4; validate with `isValidShareToken` before loading share data.

## Server changes

- New `/api` routes: rate limit + sanitize inputs + `clientSafeError` on failures.
- See `server/security.mjs` — reuse helpers, do not duplicate auth logic.

## Full policy

Read `SECURITY.md` before production deployment or auth changes.
